#, python-brace-format
msgid "Terminology bindings at the element level must be inferred from more <a0>general documentation</a0>.  The {code0} JSON-LD context introduces the {code1} element for vaccines, but there is no documentation on which codes this element is bound to or whether this is used in production. There is no other computable representation of vaccine type/product."
msgstr "元素级的术语绑定必须从更<a0>通用的文档</a0>中推断。{code0} JSON-LD 上下文为疫苗引入了 {code1} 元素，但没有文档说明该元素绑定到哪些代码，或该元素是否在生产环境中使用。疫苗类型/产品没有其他可计算的表示形式。"

#: input/pagecontent/trust_domains.md:19
msgid "Terms of use"
msgstr "使用条款"

#: input/pagecontent/trust_domains.md:65
msgid "The  <a0>IPS Pilgrimage</a0> implementation guide includes a machine-readable representation of WHO guidelines for verifiable IPS during pilgrimage. It explicitly encodes computer-interoperable logic, including data models, terminologies, and logic expressions, in a computable language to support implementation of IPS during pilgrimage usage scenario."
msgstr "<a0>IPS 朝觐</a0>实施指南包含世卫组织（WHO）关于朝觐期间可验证 IPS 的指南的机器可读表示。它以可计算语言明确编码了计算机可互操作的逻辑，包括数据模型、术语和逻辑表达式，以支持在朝觐使用场景中实施 IPS。"

#: input/pagecontent/trust_domains.md:29
msgid "The <a0>Digital Documentation of COVID-19 Certificates (DDCC)</a0> published in August 2021 and similar guidance for test results (https://www.who.int/publications/i/item/WHO-2019-nCoV-Digital_certificates_diagnostic_test_results-2022.1) published in March 2022 serve as the reference for the associated <a1>FHIR Implementation Guide</a1>. This Implementation Guide (IG) acts as the computable representation of the core data elements in the published guidance, mapped to standard terminologies. These data models, in the form of FHIR logical models, and terminologies, in the form of FHIR value sets, are the basis for interoperability between the various credential formats. The IG provides FHIR Structure Maps and Concept Maps to define transformations between supported credential formats and the core data set, which allows business rules to execute against a common set of data elements."
msgstr "2021 年 8 月发布的<a0>COVID-19 证书数字文档（DDCC）</a0>以及 2022 年 3 月发布的针对检测结果的类似指导（https://www.who.int/publications/i/item/WHO-2019-nCoV-Digital_certificates_diagnostic_test_results-2022.1）是相关 <a1>FHIR 实施指南</a1>的参考依据。本实施指南（IG）是已发布指导中核心数据元素的可计算表示，并映射到标准术语。这些以 FHIR 逻辑模型形式表示的数据模型和以 FHIR 值集形式表示的术语，是各种凭证格式之间互操作性的基础。该 IG 提供 FHIR Structure Map 和 Concept Map，用于定义所支持的凭证格式与核心数据集之间的转换，从而使业务规则能够针对一组通用数据元素执行。"

#: input/pagecontent/trust_domains.md:13
msgid "The <a0>GDHCN Administrative and Operational Framework</a0> is the legal source for Trust Domains. The <a1>Trust Domain</a1> logical model follows its three-part definition: use cases (modelled by DAK components), technical specifications, and policy and regulatory standards. A Trust Domain also names its terms of use, which is a ValueSet of the policies a participant may say it acts under."
msgstr "<a0>《GDHCN 行政与运营框架》</a0>是信任域的法律来源。<a1>信任域</a1>逻辑模型遵循其三部分定义：用例（由 DAK 组件建模）、技术规范，以及政策和监管标准。信任域还指明其使用条款，即由参与方可以声明其所遵循的政策组成的 ValueSet。"

#: input/pagecontent/trust_domains.md:61
msgid "The <a0>Pan-American Highway for Digital Health (PH4H)</a0> implementation guide describes the usage of the GDHCN for the Americas region."
msgstr "<a0>泛美数字健康高速公路（PH4H）</a0>实施指南描述了 GDHCN 在美洲区域的使用。"

#: input/pagecontent/trust_domains.md:8
msgid "The codes for the GDHCN Trust Domains are contained in the GDHCN Trust Domain Value Set."
msgstr "GDHCN 信任域的代码包含在 GDHCN 信任域值集中。"

#: input/pagecontent/trust_domains.md:17
msgid "The model allows each part to be empty, but an empty part is a QA error. So is a terms-of-use ValueSet that no BPMN business process uses."
msgstr "该模型允许每个部分为空，但空的部分属于 QA 错误。没有任何 BPMN 业务流程使用的使用条款 ValueSet 同样属于 QA 错误。"

#: input/pagecontent/trust_domains.md:4
msgid "the open, interoperable technical specifications that identify or define the applicable Trusted Services and Verifiable Digital Health Certificates; and"
msgstr "确定或定义适用的可信服务和可验证数字健康证书的开放、可互操作技术规范；以及"

